<article class="env-lemma" id="0FKK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FKK">Lemma <span data-tag="0FKK">14.28.7</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an additive category. Let $a : U \to V$ be a morphism of cosimplicial objects of $\mathcal{A}$. If $a$ is a homotopy equivalence, then $s(a) : s(U) \to s(V)$ is a homotopy equivalence of chain complexes. If in addition $\mathcal{A}$ is abelian, then also $Q(a) : Q(U) \to Q(V)$ is a homotopy equivalence of chain complexes. </p>
